      <h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.6rem,3vw,2.4rem);font-weight:300;color:#fff;margin-bottom:1rem;">A Seasonally Inverted, Freight-Distance-Aware Market</h2>
      <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:640px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;">Australia's fashion seasons run opposite to the Northern Hemisphere, which means Australian buyers often plan production schedules around a different calendar than European or US brands — a "summer" drop for Australia ships during the Northern winter. Freight distance also matters more here than in most markets: Australian buyers frequently ask about consolidated sea-freight options to reduce per-unit shipping cost on larger orders.</p>
