        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;color:#fff;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">What is DFQF and how does it benefit my imports?</h3>
        <p style="color:#FFFFFF;font-size:0.88rem;line-height:1.8;">DFQF (Duty-Free Quota-Free) is how Australia applies its System of Tariff Preferences (ASTP) to LDCs like Bangladesh. Apparel categories enter Australia at 0% duty on qualifying goods, versus 10-17.5% standard MFN rates for non-preferred countries — and Australia has officially confirmed this continues past Bangladesh's November 2026 LDC graduation.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="border-bottom:1px solid #e00;padding:1.5rem 0;">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;color:#fff;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">What documents do I need to import clothing from Bangladesh to Australia?</h3>
        <p style="color:#FFFFFF;font-size:0.88rem;line-height:1.8;">Required documents include commercial invoice, packing list, bill of lading, certificate of origin, and DFQF proof of origin for preferential duty claims. We also provide ACCC compliance certificates and Australian textile labeling documentation.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="border-bottom:1px solid #e00;padding:1.5rem 0;">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;color:#fff;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">How long does shipping from Bangladesh to Australia take?</h3>
        <p style="color:#FFFFFF;font-size:0.88rem;line-height:1.8;">Ocean freight to Sydney takes 30-35 days, to Melbourne 32-38 days. Production adds 30-45 days before shipping. Air freight reduces transit to 7-10 days for urgent orders. Weekly sailings ensure reliable delivery schedules.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="border-bottom:1px solid #e00;padding:1.5rem 0;">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;color:#fff;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">Do you comply with Australian Consumer Law and ACCC standards?</h3>
        <p style="color:#FFFFFF;font-size:0.88rem;line-height:1.8;">Yes. We maintain full compliance with Australian Consumer Law, ACCC consumer goods standards, and Product Safety Australia requirements. We provide all necessary compliance documentation including textile labeling and safety certificates.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="padding:1.5rem 0;">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;color:#fff;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">What are the Australian import duties for clothing from Bangladesh?</h3>
        <p style="color:#FFFFFF;font-size:0.88rem;line-height:1.8;">Zero. Bangladesh-origin garments enter Australia duty-free under DFQF on 100% of tariff lines, versus 10-17.5% standard MFN rates for non-preferred countries. This is officially confirmed to continue past Bangladesh's 2026 LDC graduation. We provide accurate duty documentation and tariff classification with every quote.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="border-top:1px solid #e00;padding:1.5rem 0;">
        <h3 style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;color:#fff;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">Can you plan production around Australia's inverted fashion seasons?</h3>
        <p style="color:#FFFFFF;font-size:0.88rem;line-height:1.8;">Yes. We regularly schedule bulk production to land Australian "summer" and "winter" drops on the opposite calendar to Northern Hemisphere orders — just confirm your target in-market date and we work backward from there.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

